  "question": {
    "text": "The self induced emf of a coil is <math><mn>25</mn></math> volts. When the current in it is changed at uniform rate from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> , the change in the energy of the inductance is:"
  },
