  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Induced emf / back emf in an inductor coil is given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#949;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>Ldi</mi><mi>dt</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math><br /><br />Energy of inductor is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Energy change&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>625</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>437</mn><mo>.5</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>"
